  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>This dog washing station is at the entrance of town, right next to the Avia Xpress petrol station (near Avenue de Saint-Raphaël, D559). It is a station of the Wash.ME Group brand (Wash Toutou network), with a washing tub, hose and built-in dog dryer.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>Prices and operation are those published by the brand, Wash Toutou (Wash.ME group, washtoutou.wash-megroup.com). The station works without appointment and is paid directly on the touchscreen terminal, by contactless bank card, Google Pay or Apple Pay, with no account to create. The brand announces 24/7 access for its network, while specifying that stations are available according to the hours of the site where they are installed: check for this one.</p>
      <p>The process has 4 steps: choose your programme on the screen, clean the cabin and tub if needed (a disinfectant is provided), wash and dry the dog as you wish, then leave. Two options are offered: "Small dog" at €10 for 10 minutes, or "Large dog" at €15 for 15 minutes; you can also choose your own duration from 2 to 20 minutes, at €1 per minute. Five programmes are available: shampoo, conditioner, anti-parasite treatment, rinse and drying. The water is hot (38 °C) or cold as you prefer, a non-slip mat prevents slipping, a hook lets you attach the lead and an access step helps small dogs get into the tub, which according to the brand is spacious enough for large breeds. The cycle pauses automatically if you let go of the hose, and a tub disinfection cycle is offered before and after each use. The brand announces an interface in 26 languages.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: choose the duration according to your dog's size (10 min for a small one, 15 min for a large one) and bring your towel; a coat hook and a shelf are provided in the station for your belongings.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The station is signposted at the entrance of Cavalaire-sur-Mer, near the Avia Xpress station, Avenue de Saint-Raphaël (D559). The town centre and harbour are a few minutes' drive away.</p>
